{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186815-a-time-war-setting-trimity-agon","id":1186815,"title":"A Time War setting: Trimity Agon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-16T14:12:20-08:00","id":1186815,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> A Time War setting: Trimity Agon","content":"An agon is a struggle or contest, thus a good name for a war where you might never encounter the foe and they might even end up never existing in the first place.<br /> <br /> A Time War setting would have two main game benifits and many artistic ones. The first game benefit would be bringing all the templates and settings together without blurring everything into mush. Because the crossovers would happen outside of the regular settings, those settings would stay pristine. The second benefit would be allowing alternative settings that simply don't fit the metaplot. Example: A plup SciFi future with Daredevils, Stalwarts, and Mesmerists, running around Mars or maybe the galaxy! A post-apocalyptic setting or steampunk don't fit the Trinity metaplot either, but as alternate worlds they would.<br /> <br /> I'd suggest different forms of time travel having different limitations. Mercer seems to be free of constraints other than being unable to go backwards in time. Others might face paradox like limits against changing well known events. You can't save Lincoln, but you could save an obscure individual. The change might be subtle but noticeable. Others might find the past is set in stone for them. They could learn secrets or hide there but they could never change it. Others would change everything each time they travel in time. Drifting lost amoung parallel worlds.<br /> <br /> Still, playing around with the limits of the setting and the genres it is composed of would be the main attraction. Like Doctor Who, you could swirl genres around your little finger and have a grand time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 02-23-2018, 05:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T22:05:11-08:00","id":1186937,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the misspelling. There seems to be no way to correct my mistake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T15:11:40-08:00","id":1187358,"title":"","content":"Feel free to comment or add ideas of your own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T10:07:35-08:00","id":1187589,"title":"","content":"I'm going to take this here. I think the Time war game should be the &quot;home&quot; line for Tier 3 Paramorphs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T12:57:11-08:00","id":1187626,"title":"","content":"You deserve a comment, even though my game (now) is over in the CofD area. My table is running a long-term effort that is very similar to this, and the way it's structured is: time travel (parallel world), followed by an interlude (alternate time/world), then more of the main timestream, repeat. The interludes serve to display linkages between NPCs and PC that otherwise would not come out in regular play, and permit genres and styles that are not compatible with the &quot;main&quot; stream (dark medieval fantasy). <br /> <br /> In the main stream the PCs encounter history and behind the scenes are responsible for many instances of it being &quot;as they expect it&quot;--since they are, themselves, time travelers from what we'd call the present. During interludes the PCs both learn revelations and often make things worse through their own actions, explaining how the main stream got the way it is. Methods used include McGuffin-book (Book of Thoth), dream-rituals that may or may not involve actual time-travel, projected consciousness, and the like.<br /> <br /> Confused? <br /> <br /> Example actual play:<br /> <br /> <b>2002 -&gt; 1060</b> (prelude)<br /> <b>1060-1073</b> (main stream1)<br /> <b>1073 -&gt; 2016</b> (interlude1) [in which a PC is responsible for enabling the destruction of the world by Yog-Sothoth]<br /> <b>2016 -&gt; 460/466 </b>(time bubble/loop, prelude2)<br /> <b>466-467</b> (main stream2)<br /> 1073-2 (interlude2, techno-gothic mecha-vampire Arthurian theater) [in which a PC engenders the birth of a major antagonist in main stream1/interlude1, who is inserted backwards into the flow of main stream2]<br /> 1073-2 -&gt; 467 <br /> 467-474 (main stream2)<br /> 474 -&gt; ~7000 BC-ish (interlude3, including Carcosa) [in which a PC facilitates entry within the timestream of the major antagonist, encounters pre-Tuatha-de-Dannan peoples and major plot NPCs]<br /> 7000BC -&gt; 474<br /> 474- (main stream2)<br /> <br /> And etc. there are several less-detailed interludes that I haven't bothered to plot out yet fully. Bolded items were completed in play. <br /> <br /> General thread is &quot;stamping down the end of the world&quot; and &quot;causing yourself a lot of pain.&quot;<br /> <br /> Depending on your perspective, the PCs might in fact sit on <i><b>both sides</b></i> of the Time Agon.<br /> <br /> Obviously this doesn't much connect with Trinity, except that I'm still eyeing my Aberrant book on the shelf and waiting for the opportunity to go full super-heroes on 'em!<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T14:00:03-08:00","id":1187638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186815-a-time-war-setting-trimity-agon?p=1187589#post1187589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to take this here. I think the Time war game should be the &quot;home&quot; line for Tier 3 Paramorphs.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of Tier 3 paramorphs/Talents being a primary &quot;splat&quot; for a theoretical Time War supplement actually makes a lot of sense. After all, even though nobody in the currently described eras realizes it, Talents are all about subconsciously pulling from alternate dimensions and timelines. As such, it makes sense that a sufficiently advanced one might realize that instead of pulling things through to them, they can instead push themselves into parallel timelines and dimensions, eventually being able to do full-on time travel and (presumably) dimension-hopping. This would then jive with Max Mercer still being a paramorph/Talent, he's just an exceptionally powerful one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T14:18:11-08:00","id":1187643,"title":"","content":"I'll go one step further: Teleporters are to Paramorphs as Quantakinetics are to Novas. That is, a fully-realized Paramorph isn't limited to just timelines and dimensions; she should also be able to warp space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T14:27:32-08:00","id":1187646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186815-a-time-war-setting-trimity-agon?p=1187643#post1187643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll go one step further: Teleporters are to Paramorphs as Quantakinetics are to Novas. That is, a fully-realized Paramorph isn't limited to just timelines and dimensions; she should also be able to warp space.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everyone seems to have a space buy in, though I have no problem with this idea(though would that mean there's a Quantum psi manipulation power?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T16:37:18-08:00","id":1188017,"title":"","content":"You haven't heard of the setting's Quantakinetics? The Chitra something-or-other Psi Order, who supposedly got wiped out due to being corrupted by the Aberrants?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T18:24:40-08:00","id":1188049,"title":"","content":"I may be misinterpeting, but I took Lian's comment to be asking about a Quantum power that manipulates Psi, as opposed to Quantakinesis which is a Psi power that manipulates Quantum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T00:41:41-08:00","id":1188097,"title":"","content":"Either way quantakinetics on the run could be pawns in the Time Wars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T01:57:11-08:00","id":1188110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186815-a-time-war-setting-trimity-agon?p=1187643#post1187643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Teleporters are to Paramorphs as Quantakinetics are to Novas.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m having trouble understanding what you mean. Does ffanxii4ever have it right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T05:57:42-08:00","id":1188150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186815-a-time-war-setting-trimity-agon?p=1188110#post1188110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m having trouble understanding what you mean. Does ffanxii4ever have it right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think he may be making a suggestion or a wild guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T08:39:31-08:00","id":1188182,"title":"","content":"Well all of this has got me thinking of a Tier 3 Talent / Amber-like game (if you haven't read the Amber series by Zelazny you should). Moving through variations of a reality as easily as walking. Dramatic editing allowing for handy things like your sister remembering to stash a grenade in her purse : )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","name":"yrtalien","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T13:42:09-08:00","id":1188287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186815-a-time-war-setting-trimity-agon?p=1188017#post1188017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You haven't heard of the setting's Quantakinetics? The Chitra something-or-other Psi Order, who supposedly got wiped out due to being corrupted by the Aberrants?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I meant perhaps there's a Quantum power for manipulating psi a mirror to the QK.. on the other hand perhaps its a one way direction. Quantum is more Brute Force than Psi, which is more Brute force than Talent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T19:34:53-08:00","id":1188755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yrtalien</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186815-a-time-war-setting-trimity-agon?p=1188182#post1188182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well all of this has got me thinking of a Tier 3 Talent / Amber-like game (if you haven't read the Amber series by Zelazny you should). Moving through variations of a reality as easily as walking. Dramatic editing allowing for handy things like your sister remembering to stash a grenade in her purse : )</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a logical outgrowth of a timewar book. Amber-like godlike supers fighting their own godwar would be a scary-fun faction. They could later get their own sourcebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T02:56:55-08:00","id":1188815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186815-a-time-war-setting-trimity-agon?p=1187626#post1187626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You deserve a comment, even though my game (now) is over in the CofD area. My table is running a long-term effort that is very similar to this, and the way it's structured is: time travel (parallel world), followed by an interlude (alternate time/world), then more of the main timestream, repeat. The interludes serve to display linkages between NPCs and PC that otherwise would not come out in regular play, and permit genres and styles that are not compatible with the &amp;quot;main&amp;quot; stream (dark medieval fantasy). <br /> <br /> In the main stream the PCs encounter history and behind the scenes are responsible for many instances of it being &amp;quot;as they expect it&amp;quot;--since they are, themselves, time travelers from what we'd call the present. During interludes the PCs both learn revelations and often make things worse through their own actions, explaining how the main stream got the way it is. Methods used include McGuffin-book (Book of Thoth), dream-rituals that may or may not involve actual time-travel, projected consciousness, and the like.<br /> <br /> Confused? <br /> <br /> Example actual play:<br /> <br /> <b>2002 -&gt; 1060</b> (prelude)<br /> <b>1060-1073</b> (main stream1)<br /> <b>1073 -&gt; 2016</b> (interlude1) [in which a PC is responsible for enabling the destruction of the world by Yog-Sothoth]<br /> <b>2016 -&gt; 460/466 </b>(time bubble/loop, prelude2)<br /> <b>466-467</b> (main stream2)<br /> 1073-2 (interlude2, techno-gothic mecha-vampire Arthurian theater) [in which a PC engenders the birth of a major antagonist in main stream1/interlude1, who is inserted backwards into the flow of main stream2]<br /> 1073-2 -&gt; 467 <br /> 467-474 (main stream2)<br /> 474 -&gt; ~7000 BC-ish (interlude3, including Carcosa) [in which a PC facilitates entry within the timestream of the major antagonist, encounters pre-Tuatha-de-Dannan peoples and major plot NPCs]<br /> 7000BC -&gt; 474<br /> 474- (main stream2)<br /> <br /> And etc. there are several less-detailed interludes that I haven't bothered to plot out yet fully. Bolded items were completed in play. <br /> <br /> General thread is &amp;quot;stamping down the end of the world&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;causing yourself a lot of pain.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Depending on your perspective, the PCs might in fact sit on <i><b>both sides</b></i> of the Time Agon.<br /> <br /> Obviously this doesn't much connect with Trinity, except that I'm still eyeing my Aberrant book on the shelf and waiting for the opportunity to go full super-heroes on 'em!<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope you get a grand festival of going full superhero on them. Mind you meeting the Tuatha in ancient times sounds very Jack Kirby to me. Bringing the Tautha forward to the present to fight off Yog-sothoth would be a supers game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T06:24:43-08:00","id":1188851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1186815-a-time-war-setting-trimity-agon?p=1188815#post1188815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hope you get a grand festival of going full superhero on them. Mind you meeting the Tuatha in ancient times sounds very Jack Kirby to me. Bringing the Tautha forward to the present to fight off Yog-sothoth would be a supers game.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good idea. Present PCs' meta-quest is to literally save the soul of their friend and companion, the loss of which--including the bond with the PC in Interlude1, enabled the ritual that brought forth Yog-Sothoth. Making friends in fae places and wrenching the conflict away from the real world is a viable Plan B, as is convincing the antagonist actors that this is all a very bad idea and won't get what they want! (It won't.)<br /> <br /> Since the PCs are in Arthurian times I'm sorely tempted to toss in one-shot crossovers with supers ala some of the more obscure Marvel plot arcs. Just because its an opportunity to mess with 'em.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the point is that <i><b>time is a spiral</b></i>, and in such a of campaign the PCs move in and out linearly across the stream, encountering scenarios in which the situation and/or NPCs seem to know more than they should and have encountered the PCs before. Who is chasing whom? What kind of game is afoot? And if the future is not set, then why do the antagonists not simply snuff the PCs out?<br /> <br /> The action--of which there should be plenty to distract--is actually secondary to the puzzle of what is going on. And my technique recommendation is, for the Storyteller, <i>do not answer that question for yourself</i>; you will blinker your own ability to react and inadvertently create something less engaging, more straightforward.<br /> <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T06:35:28-08:00","id":1188854,"title":"","content":"Spiral and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">Labyrinths</a> are linked ideas. Walking a labyrinth is about moving from A to A in order to actually know A in the first place. Their spiral path needs to show them who they are/were/could be. Or am I getting to artsy here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T06:36:03-07:00","id":1199022,"title":"","content":"What do people think of the idea that your metaphor for the nature of time both empowers and limits your time travel abilities?<br /> <br /> Example: If time is a river, then it takes more energy to go against the current than with it. Thus travel to the most likely future would be easy. Whereas travel to odd corners of the past would be exhausting.<br /> <br /> If time is an endless series of branching corridors, getting lost is a serious risk.<br /> <br /> Change your metaphore change your strengths and weaknesses. However, the more powerful and or experienced a time traveller you are, the more your metaphor is part of you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T12:40:46-07:00","id":1199452,"title":"","content":"The ins and outs of the timewar would leave for lots of eddies and currents. Some of the backwaters might be dangerous because their inhabitants fear being left high and dry. Attackers from fading or otherwise endangered realities could have strange powers or combinations of powers. Interesting threats and challenges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-09T06:04:34-07:00","id":1226061,"title":"","content":"Is there anything in the published materials so far that would support or thwart a time travel game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T05:38:51-07:00","id":1226744,"title":"","content":"Time Travel was a power in the Aberrant players guide in 1st ed. That counts as support right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T11:15:05-07:00","id":1226857,"title":"","content":"Not really; 2e isn't 1e, and the Time Travel Quantum Power is not guaranteed to make a return.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T23:44:09-07:00","id":1227822,"title":"","content":"True, but we don't have Aberrant 2e and the far future setting (1000+ after \u00c6on) is the most likely place to find time travel, either Quantum or paramorph based. Since the later is way off and it is unlikely to show up in the former (noted by being from a supplement), it is likely to be as close to an official word for quite some time.<br /> <br /> We might see the Crosstime Travel power make a return though, as it plays into the powers of Talents and the description of the Continuum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T11:46:27-07:00","id":1261338,"title":"","content":"And even if neither Time Travel nor Crosstime Travel make an official appearance there's still the old Aberrant/Trinity games. Hopefully there will be a &quot;conversion manual&quot; to allow people to play out there favorite modules from old Trinity/Aberrant under the new rules. So you could get at those powers that way. Or just look at how various Abberant powers are modeled under the new system and figure out a conversion yourself. If you know how &quot;Quantum Bolt&quot; works (in terms of range, area, duration, effect, etc.) in the old and new systems and you know what &quot;Crosstime Travel&quot; looked like in the old system, you should be able to model it for the new system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}